A||||8||RiceCooker||The Good, the Bad, & the Ugly||||6||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||05-22-2001||02:54 PM||||Well, the building excitement finally brought the May long weekend (Victoria day in Canada)<P>Me and some friends go camping every year to a place called Westward Ho (no jokes on that name).<P>The good: We had tons of fun on Thursday night since i got friday off work too for an extra long weekend. I cleaned up the RiceCooker real nice and got tons of comments from complete strangers. My favorite is getting them to try and guess how old it is. "15 years!!!??? wow, that's in good shape, etc etc." I just try to hide my grin and say thanks cause i'm so proud of my car.<P>Well we had our guitars - i just bought my acoustic bass last week after i got a surprise bonus from my work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> All in all we had two nights of fun and lotsa beer.<P>The bad: Well there was an Alberta wide fire ban so no sittin by the campfire all night and it was quite chilly. Lots more people showed up on Friday, freinds of friends that i didnt really know to well and of course they were a bunch of tough guys. I slept throught the whole thing (i kinda thought i was dreaming cause i heard it. These guys were picking fights and tons of people were there with RCMP (police) and yelling and i was hoping nothing (like my car) was damaged.<P>The Ugly: MY FACE Saturday morning - 7:00 a.m. getting woken up by the wardens kicking us all out - EVEN me and my friends who had no clue what happened. So i drove home and relaxed/recovered saturday and Sunday had another great night playin music and writing songs. <P>Well that's my camping story - we're gonna have to go again without those trouble makers and when there is no fire ban. <P>smiles,<BR>Todd<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004312.html" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004312.html</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||loafer87gt||05-22-2001||03:13 PM||||Sounds like a 'memorable' weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Where the hell is Westward Ho? Our weekend plans kinda fell to pieces. A couple of my buddies and I had all of our stuff loaded up into the Jeep and were ready to head out to Sylvain Lake, AB, but we blew a tire about an hour out of town. Being as 44 inch mudders are to cheap to replace, and none of us other guys had a vehicle that could haul everyone around in, we ended up just heading up to a lake nearby. What sucked is that after the tire incident, and sitting around trying to figure out what the heck to do, we didn't get to the bar at the lake till 2:10, ten minutes after last call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Everything turned out Millhouse tho, some chick heard me pleading to the bartender, explaing our dilemna, and took pitty on me and invited us back to her and her friends campsite. SCORE! It sounds like we planning on heading up to Sylvain the Canada day weekend, you ever been there, it is supposed to rock.||||reg||1
Z||000002||saleenfiero||05-22-2001||03:18 PM||||I hear you guys, we went out to Elkwater (Cypress Hills - Alberta side), and I didn't really think the fire ban would hamper much of the fun, but DAMN, it sucked.  I guess this is supposed to be off topic, but I thought I would add my experience.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||05-22-2001||03:20 PM||||Yeah, I know where Sylvan Lake is and supposedly it is one of the hottest chic spots in the country for May long weekend.<P>They did have a big time storm there on Saturday so you missed that. <P>Westward Ho is close to Sundre which is about 1/2 southwest of Red Deer.<P>Keep me posted on the Canada Day Sylvan lake thing - meeting up with an out of province PFF'er would be sweet.<P>It'd be a huge shaker for sure - nobody knows how to party like us Fieroholics, EH?<P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||RiceCooker||05-22-2001||03:22 PM||||Oops, sorry this is definatley off topic. <P>I guess i was supposed to talk more about how a cleanup up my Fiero and how everyone gawked at it all weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
